{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100877","id":2254257495,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6GXT1X","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100877","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100877.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100877.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100877","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100877/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100877/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100877/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d2d02d0ea8a1edcb4518807612f24c0ae9c8fc2b","number":100877,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"EditorNode: Add function to load file as either scene or resource","user":{"login":"larspet","id":16100387,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTAwMzg3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16100387?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet","html_url":"https://github.com/larspet","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/larspet/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"There were many instances where either `EditorNode::load_scene()`/`open_request()` or `load_resource()` was called depending on if the file was a `PackedScene` or not. This PR is meant to simplify those cases and make the `PackedScene` checks more consistent. This also led to some minor bug fixes related to reopening closed scene tabs with the `Ctrl+Shift+T` command.\r\n\r\n### Add `EditorNode::load_scene_or_resource()`\r\n\r\n\r\nI was unsure if I should add this new function, or instead allow `load_resource()` to load scenes as well (instead of simply inspecting the `PackedScene` resource). Additionally, `load_resource()` could then have a new parameter `p_open_if_scene`, deciding between opening or inspecting.\r\n\r\n### Remove `EditorNode::open_request()`\r\n`open_request()` did two things:\r\n1. Remove scene from previous scenes list.\r\n2. Call `load_scene()`.\r\n\r\nThis meant that directly calling `load_scene()` would not update the previous scenes history. I removed `open_request()` and moved the updating of previous scenes  to `load_scene()` instead.\r\n\r\n### Refactor previous scenes logic\r\n\r\n- Rename related variables/functions to `prev_closed_scenes` to differentiate from `recent_scenes`.\r\n- Enable or disable `FILE_OPEN_PREV` menu_item/shortcut directly when updating previous scene list (instead of just after opening/closing the Scene menu.\r\n- Remove `opening_prev` member variable. It has no purpose and just caused clutter by setting it to `false` everywhere.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.